<title>SINGAPORE: Hwa Hong 1996 net profit up 11.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Hwa Hong 1996 net profit up 11.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to 31 December, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   10.96     vs    9.82</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)			4.00     vs    4.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		   7.50     vs    6.70</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents) 7.40     vs    6.70</p>
<p>    Turnover			    275.54     vs  210.29</p>
<p>    Investment income		   1.29     vs    0.90</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest     3.60     vs    4.31</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.73     vs    0.80</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	    2.21     vs    2.27</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	   4.51     vs    3.79</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		     11.06     vs    9.99</p>
<p>    Tax				     4.60     vs    3.96</p>
<p>    Minorities		 (loss)   0.02     vs    0.01  (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	  (loss)   0.05     vs    0.54  (gain)</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		  24 July 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		 8 July 1997</p>
<p>Note - Hwa Hong Corp Ltd has interests in insurance, warehouse rentals, packaging of edible oil products, trading in consumer products and piling and construction.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
